From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:47:08 +0900
Subject: Wayland backend: send the GPU completion fence to a host without
 implicit synchronization

When the render device's buffers have no implicit synchronization (WaylandBackend::implicitSync(),
the Android host's AHardwareBuffers) and the host offers zwp_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1,
export an EGL native fence for each output frame and attach it with set_acquire_fence in the
same commit; the render thread no longer blocks in glFinish. Without the global, or without a
native fence, it still waits. Measured on the Android host: Paint p50 6.7 -> 2.0 ms (docs/57).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic for nested KWin on hosts with explicit synchronization and without implicit sync]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:perf.compositor
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/57 docs/72
Origin: vendor, commit:5127264a
